  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_62eb93056464485a8a17440a7cd20a62",
      "statement": "The `toolIntegrations` namespace is backed by `ToolIntegrationsGateway`, a `TypertRemoteService` subclass registered on the host face via `apply()` (`ctx.plugin(ToolIntegrationsGateway)`). It injects `['loader']`, binds its wire namespace to `toolIntegrations` in its constructor (`super(ctx, 'toolIntegrations')`), and exposes four `@Remote` methods — `list`, `read`, `write`, `delete` — that the browser client consumes through the mounted Typert remote.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/client/remote.ts#L166-L170",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5555a904b551d2ecda0428ce96b02bb71fd774e3a9c92b6719c04318b2f59d0e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L1465-L1473",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db4df7bc6e7b625642ca9de07581ec29dad32b152162bd8c6040933385220091:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L222-L233",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4778fc636b82e2937ee6d682cf7b1c62e334235d9e4cbdfe0422a5f2ae2060be:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1e660d5550264fc0a2d4166c4ff4ccee",
      "statement": "The `mounted` map — `private mounted = new Map<string, string>()` mapping `serverName` → loader entry id — is the authoritative source of whether a configured MCP server is live. `list()` derives each item's `mounted` flag directly from it (`this.mounted.has(c.serverName)`), so the config file being present never implies the server's tools are actually available; a saved-but-not-mounted server reports `mounted: false`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L435-L435",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e2475800704bc3dbdc5ab89f515326a332e38d8a9764539a7bae58dad9c4f5c3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L494-L498",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4ccccb2953cb6a6458e6079aefaec6372d39ffbb7dfaf5cdd0df8e27e04b556:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6de47ad01e214da3b1266c4db33d1444",
      "statement": "The MCP config is persisted to a per-profile `mcp-servers.json`. `MCP_FILE()` derives the active profile freshly from `process.argv` on every call via `profileNameFromArgv`, returning `dshHomePath('profiles', profile, 'mcp-servers.json')` when a profile is active, else the global `dshHomePath('mcp-servers.json')`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L414-L417",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7232a386bf96c5a296b3de275e2994689fc39407709c15d5c07fce24d4717629:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L566-L578",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:82a299fe918c08e17951114060302e7f59459685aa6c071fca5464df485d6c3b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cdcc8c884cc44483a35a603f18a4d3d1",
      "statement": "The file is a flat JSON **array** of `McpConfig` objects, not a name-keyed map. `loadConfigs()` returns `[]` when the file is absent or unparseable (a fresh profile is not an error), and `saveConfigs()` `mkdir`s the dsh home `recursive: true` then writes the array as 2-space-indented JSON. `read` finds by `serverName` (throwing `mcp server not found` when absent), `write` replace-or-pushes at the found index, and `delete` filters the array out.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L444-L457",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28104dc9dc671e8d104ddb27cb7218a69063fbd7361be926f2dadeef47e8d394:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L500-L513",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:13054cfc2fb7851ae49b9384a50174612f39edf592e1ed86671bee16755e4646:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L527-L534",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:572b757ca1a7a5248f4b04b60aed72002b2727914249acb2ba9bca9d332032af:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_31da0d2046954343a87bf350a319c382",
      "statement": "The `McpConfig` shape discriminates by `transport: 'stdio' | 'streamable-http'`. `command`/`args`/`env`/`cwd` describe a `stdio` server, while `url`/`headers` describe a `streamable-http` server; all transport-specific fields are optional and only the matching branch is populated. The client `McpConfig` interface and the host interface mirror each other exactly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/client/ToolIntegrationsView.tsx#L10-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7e8a018d728cd2c13a369ac3262cb8d39e198a7e0dc63d2f494d74780981f2a6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L420-L429",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7e8a018d728cd2c13a369ac3262cb8d39e198a7e0dc63d2f494d74780981f2a6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_edc19f4e7c924a498792eb8d32fcff76",
      "statement": "`entryFor(cfg)` turns a config into a loader entry with a deterministic id `mcp-<serverName>` and `name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client'` (the `MCP_CLIENT` constant), passing the original config (minus `serverName`, re-added as `serverName`) into the entry. Because the id is derived from the serverName, the `mounted` map's key/value pairing is self-consistent and the hot-replace's remove-then-create is predictable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L418-L418",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:928aeba594dd316c9db6449404696aee8fd8c564c73780e18b5a197a8c5b6f75:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L474-L481",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:835ad5d11a85fdb1a07b53ab62a80cedf95d5549e7111a3f38644991d5af9bd7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_360aa766eba14e3b9523e36a59129ead",
      "statement": "Startup mounting is non-blocking: the `ToolIntegrationsGateway` constructor fires `void this.mountAll().catch(() => {})`, so construction never waits on loader creation. `mountAll()` loops over loaded configs and each `loader.create` is wrapped in its own `try/catch`; a single failing mount deletes that serverName from `mounted` (so it shows `mounted: false`) and continues, so one server failing to mount does not fail the others.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L437-L442",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:81603ae47b06dc8a3251d181d550186b6c7f42847948e3748a55d88a68cca783:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L460-L472",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:909e823506b427df3e879f76efbb344a20aac4e3901113e04bb35e4b93f06f6b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d9ece6686f4548f9afb8a8a86b0fc45e",
      "statement": "`write()` performs the live hot-replace: persist the config first (replace-or-push then `saveConfigs`), unmount the old entry via `this.unmount(serverName)`, then `loader.create(this.entryFor(config))` and record the new id in `mounted`. The new mount is isolated in `try/catch`; on failure the serverName is deleted from `mounted` but the method still returns `{ serverName }` — the save succeeded and the disk config is authoritative, so the failure is surfaced through the `mounted` flag rather than as a rejection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L508-L525",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0906ae9e7e1d09183c686c9c1f23f353b6fec01cae95a94211aed8617acfbf19:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_15abe0aae8d243ada7f36febb0dfbb55",
      "statement": "`unmount(serverName)` uses a `try/finally`: it looks up the mounted loader id and, when present, calls `loader.remove(id)` inside `try`, then unconditionally `mounted.delete(serverName)` in `finally`. This guarantees the `mounted` map never retains a stale id even if `loader.remove` throws.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L483-L492",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b26ede0bbc245cc9b20dfb96ebec2c0ab2ceb075e8da2fdb3e7d37865927ee6e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_15b29572ce8d40a9b5276080462213fb",
      "statement": "`delete()` removes the config and then unmounts the live entry. Because `unmount()` is a no-op when the server was already unmounted (no id in the `mounted` map), the loader side of `delete` is idempotent; the view confirms with `window.confirm(...)` that the server's tools will immediately become invalid.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/client/ToolIntegrationsView.tsx#L149-L162",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:385cc2f3e0d2298ba46bf3fb614a1a5a0c433605b167269875f06221d3f473f0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L527-L534",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:572b757ca1a7a5248f4b04b60aed72002b2727914249acb2ba9bca9d332032af:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_39031c393d8f43c1bf9dc58e897f1394",
      "statement": "On the client face, `registerCapabilityViews` builds `mcpApi` by wrapping each `ctx.remote.toolIntegrations.<method>()` call in `unwrap()` (which collapses the `{ ok, value } | { ok, error }` envelope and throws on `ok: false`), then injects it into the `conversation.view` slot row with `id: 'tool-integrations'` and `order: 40`. A host failure such as `read('not-present')` thus surfaces as the view's inline error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/client/index.ts#L107-L112",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d528613fe2cc898176982dd572d8f64f64ed1decd2474662b39e5c5e2cd656ea:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/client/index.ts#L129-L136",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5c5771f6ffe35a2022d2da746973812e9086bf3e04bcb21c3a491f011bfe71f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_97a2c51819ac4e1ebb06bb783f733872",
      "statement": "The client `toolIntegrations` namespace follows the same load-order constraint as the other namespaces: the `TYPERT_REMOTE` manifest must be `$mount`ed onto `ctx.remote` before the child plugin that injects `remote.toolIntegrations` runs. `apply()` mounts the manifest first, then defers capability-view registration to a child plugin whose inject list includes `remote.toolIntegrations`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/client/index.ts#L192-L193",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:348f38bb22c110b8c1cab350cdbc44379b5e5895573104fb8d1b1852466f3c6b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/client/index.ts#L231-L237",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:08c938c9c4ba4ee4fbc0b80aa3d97ce43eb2954965db180cea97c50ea9c97fe9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7d77949db1504f7a85e506c25ea6ea9b",
      "statement": "`ToolIntegrationsView` validates the `serverName` against `/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$/` before saving (bailing with an inline error otherwise), builds the `McpConfig` with only the transport-matching fields (splitting `args` by newline, parsing `env`/`headers` as key=value-per-line via `parsePairs`/`stringifyPairs`), and keeps the `serverName` input read-only while editing so the replace-and-mount in `write` keys off a stable identity.",
      "evidence": [
